BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
CASE NO: W.P. No. 20114 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010678912026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice N. Anand Venkatesh

PARTIES:
Chennai Information Technology Employees Union
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Union of India & State of Tamil Nadu, Labour Department
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Tamil Nadu Shops and Establishments Act 1947, Occupational Safety and Health Code 2020

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
Article 21, Article 19\(1\)\(g\), TN Shops Act Section 14

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Right to Disconnect, Digital Burnout, Workplace Mental Health, Article 21, Working Hours

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Petition seeking guidelines against mandatory off-hours electronic communication by employers causing psychological distress.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Does continuous digital connectivity outside contracted working hours violate the right to health under Article 21?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Unregulated electronic intrusions outside working hours violate employees' fundamental right to health and dignity under Article 21.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Right to disconnect recognized as facet of mental health under Art. 21.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice N. Anand Venkatesh
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
